# FreeIPA — Windows NSSM Configuration
# ======================================
#
# !! NOT APPLICABLE !!
#
# FreeIPA is a Linux-only service. It cannot be installed or run on Windows.
# FreeIPA relies on Linux-specific subsystems including:
#
#   - 389 Directory Server (LDAP backend)
#   - MIT Kerberos KDC
#   - BIND DNS
#   - Dogtag Certificate Authority (Java/Tomcat)
#   - Apache HTTPD (Web UI)
#   - SSSD (System Security Services Daemon)
#
# These components have no native Windows equivalents and are not portable.
#
# Windows Integration Options
# ----------------------------
# Windows machines can JOIN an existing FreeIPA domain as clients using:
#
#   1. Samba Winbind — allows Windows-style domain membership via the
#      trust relationship between FreeIPA and an Active Directory trust.
#      See: https://www.freeipa.org/page/Active_Directory_trust_setup
#
#   2. FreeIPA–Active Directory Trust — establish a cross-realm trust so
#      that Windows clients authenticate against their existing AD while
#      sharing the Kerberos realm with FreeIPA Linux hosts.
#
#   3. LDAP client libraries — Windows applications can query the FreeIPA
#      LDAP server (port 389/636) directly for user lookups.
#
# FreeIPA Server Requirements
# ----------------------------
# - RHEL 8/9, CentOS Stream 8/9, Fedora, Rocky Linux, AlmaLinux
# - systemd init system
# - x86_64 architecture
# - Minimum 2 GB RAM (4 GB recommended for production)
# - Fully qualified hostname resolvable in DNS
#
# For installation instructions, see: ../../../install/README.md
# For service management on Linux, see: ../README.md
